From 828db6617e76b82c660993b8ae0859f2ea3531bc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: steelhead99x <steelhead99x@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 11:40:37 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix(oprf): build VOPRF without std

VOPRF's batches are `Vec`s, which bare-metal targets (`target_os =
"none"`, built without std) do not get from the prelude, so
`thumbv6m-none-eabi` stopped compiling once the OPRF landed. Import it
from `alloc` there, as ML-DSA does.

Co-authored-by: Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com>
---
 rind/src/high/oprf/voprf.rs | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/rind/src/high/oprf/voprf.rs b/rind/src/high/oprf/voprf.rs
index 72f4e70c..5c2a822f 100644
--- a/rind/src/high/oprf/voprf.rs
+++ b/rind/src/high/oprf/voprf.rs
@@ -3,6 +3,8 @@
 //! RFC 9497's VOPRF mode: the OPRF, with the server proving it evaluated
 //! every blinded element in a batch with the key it published.
 
+#[cfg(target_os = "none")]
+use alloc::vec::Vec;
 use core::fmt;
 
 use super::{
